  "term": "PHR",
  "definition": "PHR refers to the platelet-to-high-density lipoprotein cholesterol ratio, a biomarker discussed as reflecting thrombosis-related cardiovascular risk. In this source, it is also described as relevant to mental health because changes in platelet activity and HDL-C may be linked with anxiety symptoms.",
